---
import Components from "@component-utils/renderBlock.astro";

const { sections } = Astro.props;
---

<!--
  Renders a page's block tree for both shells (`Page.astro`, `LibraryLayout`).

  `data-prop` is this component's own `sections` prop, which is right and has
  to stay that way: paths inside a component region resolve against the
  component's props, and the shell's `data-prop-<key>` is what maps `sections`
  back to its own frontmatter key — `pageSections` on the site,
  `contentSections` in the docs.

  Naming the frontmatter key here instead looks tidier and is fatal. `pageSections`
  is not a key of this component's props, so the array resolves to nothing and
  the editor replaces the whole page with "expect to receive a value of type
  array but instead received undefined". The error that prompted that change
  printed the path as `pageSections.sections.4.heading`, which is the editor
  showing both hops of a chain that was working; the fault was a heading bound
  on a section that had none.

  The wrapper cannot live here: the editor's re-render would nest a second
  copy of the region inside the first. Search indexing is the shell's business
  too — the site shell marks the wrapper as a Pagefind body, the docs shell
  deliberately does not.
-->
<div
  data-editable="array"
  data-prop="sections"
  data-component-key="_component"
>
  <Components contentSections={sections} />
</div>
